==English==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|la|coitus||sexual intercourse}} + {{m|la|interruptus||interrupted, cut short}}, the [[perfect passive participle]] of {{m|la|interrumpo||to interrupt, to [[cut short]]}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|head=coitus interruptus}}

# [[sexual intercourse|Sexual intercourse]] [[interrupted]] by [[withdrawal]] of the [[penis]] before [[ejaculation]].
#: {{coordinate terms|en|coitus reservatus}}
#* '''2002''', {{w|Colin Jones (historian)|Colin Jones}}, ''The Great Nation'', Penguin 2003, p. 351:
#*: Yet in the event, population continued to grow – even though signs began to appear that '''coitus interruptus''' was beginning to be used systematically to reduce family size.
#* {{quote-web|en|url=http://www.theguardian.com/society/2003/oct/07/lifeandhealth.medicineandhealth|title=Men on the pill? Yeah, right|date=2003-10-07|author=Lucy Atkins|work=The Guardian|passage=We have come some way since sheep's bladder condoms but male contraceptive options are still pretty basic. Not counting one Chinese invention - a small electronic device worn in the underpants, which causes infertility for a month after a current is switched on briefly - it is still down to the old favourites: abstinence, '''coitus interruptus''', condoms or vasectomy.}}

